From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:23:08 +0200
Subject: nv30: on the PS3, an index buffer's move to GART keeps it coherent,
 fills it by the CPU when it can, and drops one draw rather than a submission

0070's move of an index buffer from VRAM to GART left the buffer with an empty valid range and
no write fence, so a CPU write or read right after it skipped the wait for the GPU's copy. ps3rsx
also refuses a draw whose indices a GPU write earlier in the same submission touched, and refuses
an index buffer in VRAM. Before every indexed draw on the PS3 now (nv30_idxbuf_to_gart):

- A buffer in GART is CPU-written from then on (cpu_only), whatever made it there (stream usage,
  no bind, a VRAM allocation that fell back to GART), and a GPU write into it still queued in
  this submission (a staging copy before it was cpu_only, a CopyBufferSubData into it) is kicked
  first, so the kernel waits for it instead of refusing the draw.
- A buffer in VRAM whose system memory copy is current is filled into new GART storage by the
  CPU: no GPU copy, no kick, nothing to wait for; the system memory copy is freed.
- Otherwise the GPU copies it, alone in a submission. Until that copy has run the buffer is
  GPU-written: its whole range valid, its fences that submission's, GPU_WRITING set, so a
  BufferSubData right after it waits. A stale system memory copy is freed. If the copy's
  submission is cancelled, the buffer keeps its VRAM storage and moves at a later draw.
- With no room in GART the GPU's work is waited for once and the allocation tried again. A buffer
  that still can't move (no room, a lost copy, a shared buffer) costs only its draw, which is
  dropped, instead of the whole submission the kernel would refuse.

The software TNL path maps a buffer the GPU is still writing synchronized (nv30_render_vbo), so it
never reads new GART storage before the copy has filled it. NV30_PS3_IDX_STATS=1 prints a line
each time the moves of a kind pass a power of two; NV30_PS3_IDX_GART=0 or NV30_PS3_FP_GART=0 on
the PS3 prints a line that ps3rsx refuses that placement. The kick after a GPU copy makes room
first (PUSH_SPACE).

Other contexts sharing a moved vertex buffer keep its old address until they validate their
arrays again (as for any reallocation in nouveau).

Forwarded: no

